      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151497,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> spindle cell epithelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151498,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151499,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are located at the posterior and distal vaginal wall close to the hymen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151500,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients are asymptomatic or report nonspecific symptoms related to a mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151501,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare vaginal neoplasms. Patients present over a wide age range (mean: 40&nbsp;years) {15154010; 25998318; 7682380}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151502,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151503,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151504,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mixed tumours typically range in size from 15&nbsp;to 50&nbsp;mm and are solid, soft, rubbery, and mostly well circumscribed.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151505,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mixed tumours are typically well circumscribed and variably cellular and composed of spindled and epithelial elements in varying proportions and arrangements. A cellular spindle cell component, with fascicular, corded, nested, and/or reticular growths, typically predominates and is sharply demarcated from the epithelial elements, which may be glandular (typically mucinous) or comprise mature squamous epithelium; sometimes there is an admixture of glandular and squamous epithelium {15154010; 7682380}. Eosinophilic hyaline material, sometimes in the form of globules, may be present within a myxomatous or collagenous stroma. The cells show minimal nuclear atypia, and mitotic activity varies, although it is usually low. There is often coexpression of a variety of epithelial and mesenchymal markers, including AE1/AE3, CK7, EMA, CD10, SMA, desmin, h-caldesmon, WT1, calretinin, BCL2, and CD34 {15154010; 25998318; 7682380}. S100 and SOX10 are typically negative. The spindle cell elements typically strongly express epithelial markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151506,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151507,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151508,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> well-circumscribed tumour composed of morphologically benign epithelial (glandular and/or squamous) and spindle cell components.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151509,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign tumours and are not staged.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151510,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign lesions but may recur if incompletely excised.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
